## Methodology

### 1. Data Exploration
- Initial data inspection and quality assessment
- Analysis of pricing patterns across different delivery scenarios
- Correlation analysis between features and pricing
- Temporal patterns (time of day, day of week, seasonality)

### 2. Data Cleaning & Preprocessing
- Handling missing values and outliers
- Feature engineering (e.g., rush hour indicators, distance bins, demand scores)
- Data normalization and scaling
- Train/test split for model validation

### 3. Analysis & Modeling
- Exploratory analysis of key pricing drivers
- Feature importance analysis
- Model development and comparison (e.g., Linear Regression, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting)
- Model evaluation and validation
- Price elasticity analysis

### 4. Key Findings
- **Finding 1:** [Brief description - e.g., "Peak hours (6-9 PM) show 35% higher average delivery prices"]
- **Finding 2:** [Brief description - e.g., "Distance is the primary driver, accounting for 60% of price variance"]
- **Finding 3:** [Brief description - e.g., "Weather conditions significantly impact pricing during extreme events"]

